    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d800">

                <pb facs="0700" n="690" sameAs="frus:frus1949v08/pg690"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">701.0093/5–1949: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister-Counselor of Embassy in China</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Clark</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Canton</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-05-19T09:00:00+08:00">May 19, 1949—9 a.
                            m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 12:04 p. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Cantel 414, FonOff now in process burning portion their files and packing
                    remainder for shipment. Junior officers have been told that bulk of them are to
                    go Chungking with small number sent Taipei.</p>
                <pb facs="0701" n="691" xml:id="pg691"/>
                <p>Section FonOff which arranged movement Diplomatic Corps Canton states their
                    belief Chinese Government does not now have facilities move even small number
                    diplomats presently Canton to Chungking.</p>
                <p>Sent Department Cantel 414; repeated Nanking 304, Shanghai 256.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Clark</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
